WEBVTT

00:29:59.028 --> 00:30:00.907
before I demoralized them.

00:30:01.425 --> 00:30:04.353
And that was a race I typically lost.

00:30:04.377 --> 00:30:07.363
AG: He kept betting on candidates
who looked great on paper,

00:30:07.387 --> 00:30:09.963
but soon, instead of collaborating
to solve problems,

00:30:09.987 --> 00:30:11.701
they would just end up complaining,

00:30:11.725 --> 00:30:13.550
and eventually poisoning the culture.

00:30:13.574 --> 00:30:15.011
RS: Within three months,

00:30:15.035 --> 00:30:16.618
I'd catch them in the kitchen,

00:30:16.642 --> 00:30:19.996
pissing and moaning at the water cooler
with somebody else on the team.

00:30:20.020 --> 00:30:21.946
And I'm like, "What happened?

00:30:21.970 --> 00:30:23.179
How did I miss here?

00:30:23.203 --> 00:30:25.645
I thought I was hiring good people."

00:30:26.251 --> 00:30:28.305
AG: Rich went back to the drawing board,

00:30:28.329 --> 00:30:30.234
and one of his colleagues had an idea.